# Next.js Data Layer

## Server actions pattern

Actions live in `src/actions/` (not only `src/app/`). Use `actionClient` from `src/lib/safe-action.ts`:

```typescript
'use server';
import { actionClient } from '@/lib/safe-action';
import { requireSession } from '@/lib/org-server';
import { updateUserProfile } from '@/services/profile.service';

export const updateProfileAction = actionClient
  .schema(updateProfileSchema)
  .action(async ({ parsedInput }) => {
    const session = await requireSession();
    await updateUserProfile(session.user.id, { /* ... */ });
    revalidatePath('/profile');
    return { name: parsedInput.name };
  });
```

## Auth in actions

- Use `requireSession()` / `requireOrganization()` from `org-server.ts` inside actions
- Call `requireOrgPermission()` before member/invitation/settings mutations
- See `better-auth-multitenancy.mdc` for full auth/org file map

## Services

- Business logic in `src/services/` throws `ForbiddenError` / `NotFoundError` from `tenant-guard.ts`
- Services throw user-friendly errors that TanStack Query can catch and display

## Client integration

- Use `useAction` from `next-safe-action/hooks` for form submissions (see `profile-form.tsx`)
- TanStack Query: `QueryClientProvider` in `providers.tsx`; use `useQuery` when client caching is needed
- `ActionResponse<T>` type in `src/types/actions.ts` for non-safe-action returns

## Validation & error handling

- Use next-safe-action for all server actions with Zod input schemas
- Model expected errors as return values; avoid try/catch for expected errors in actions
- Use `useActionState` with react-hook-form for form validation where appropriate
- Use error boundaries for unexpected errors (`error.tsx`, `global-error.tsx`)
- Prioritize error handling at function entry with guard clauses and early returns
- Place the happy path last; avoid unnecessary `else` after early returns
- Implement user-friendly error messages; use custom error types (`ForbiddenError`, `NotFoundError`) for consistency

